1,2}=[\\begin{aligned}5\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ -2\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ \\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d4c1a7b-2341-5b8c-8112-0290f8eda65f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Block Diagonalization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e88a1f28-6563-53d3-bc3d-708493b5c121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372891} {:answer/id #uuid "4ce81622-4e88-54b0-ba9d-93e1c85c21c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372892} {:answer/id #uuid "b0f38560-e6bd-5de9-a2e8-b7acf41f77d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372893} {:answer/id #uuid "72ce22a3-c97c-51e4-b170-152fac3abe35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372894} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbacb88-8b45-56fb-92b0-0d62f8265c50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bbacb88-8b45-56fb-92b0-0d62f8265c50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372895} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc75e988-855e-59b6-ac76-61d93cef8ab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df2ca89a-9776-5dd2-9c3c-16431b4bc152" :question/math-academy-id "q-135529" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a block diagonal matrix $B,$ where the $2\\times 2$ block represents a rotation-scaling matrix, such that $A=PB{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A$ is a real $3\\times 3$ matrix that has one real eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}$ with corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and two complex eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{3}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{3},$ then $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) \\\\ 0 & -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & \\text{Re}({v}_{2}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nTo compute the eigenvalues of $A,$ we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((-2-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-1(-5)) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +13) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the real eigenvalue is \n${\\lambda }_{1}=2.$\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{2,3} & =\\frac{-6\\pm \\sqrt{(6)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 13}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =-3\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the block diagonal matrix is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d4c1a7b-2341-5b8c-8112-0290f8eda65f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Block Diagonalization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d121affa-6223-5616-a45b-f88b847de079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372898} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2bbfda-739f-55cb-99f3-42d0daa04bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372899} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb5af56-d72d-5f8e-969b-97999213c3a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372900} {:answer/id #uuid "8781ea21-86f2-593c-a8fd-fff554023d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372901} {:answer/id #uuid "f31a7313-0da5-5a2a-a6f8-0849756deaad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8781ea21-86f2-593c-a8fd-fff554023d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372901} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7fc372e-cf87-5632-b3de-798ae1fc53ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c18b932-d065-514d-8f96-aca2dbdfa575" :question/math-academy-id "q-135530" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a block diagonal matrix $B,$ where the $2\\times 2$ block represents a rotation-scaling matrix, such that $A=PB{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A$ is a real $3\\times 3$ matrix that has one real eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}$ with corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and two complex eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{3}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{3},$ then $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) \\\\ 0 & -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & \\text{Re}({v}_{2}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nTo compute the eigenvalues of $A,$ we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )((2-\\lambda )^{2}-4(-9)) & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +40) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the real eigenvalue is \n${\\lambda }_{1}=5.$\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{2,3} & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 40}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{-144}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 12\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\pm 6\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the block diagonal matrix is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d4c1a7b-2341-5b8c-8112-0290f8eda65f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Block Diagonalization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf5fba50-c458-5fde-a677-61f411090bb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372905} {:answer/id #uuid "f6609d4f-c437-5c3a-9a3f-150fa8b9a35d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372906} {:answer/id #uuid "ad59ed4a-19ed-5439-9524-48f05f031ef8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372907} {:answer/id #uuid "32c6ee3c-a745-55c8-b8c8-b0d37d87609a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372908} {:answer/id #uuid "9d24f472-819d-5726-af78-87e12d1ac840" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32c6ee3c-a745-55c8-b8c8-b0d37d87609a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372908} :answer-field/id #uuid "95b922af-5fed-5253-94ab-6192f8b266bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9bc74b4f-50af-5719-9f07-2046dc509d7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-135532" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a block diagonal matrix $B,$ where the $2\\times 2$ block represents a rotation-scaling matrix, such that $A=PB{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A$ is a real $3\\times 3$ matrix that has one real eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}$ with corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and two complex eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{3}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{3},$ then $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) \\\\ 0 & -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & \\text{Re}({v}_{2}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nTo compute the eigenvalues of $A,$ we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 6-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (6-\\lambda )((-1-\\lambda )^{2}-9(-1)) & =0 \\\\ (6-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the real eigenvalue is \n${\\lambda }_{1}=6.$\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{2,3} & =\\frac{-2\\pm \\sqrt{(2)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 10}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm \\sqrt{-36}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm 6\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\pm 3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the block diagonal matrix is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d4c1a7b-2341-5b8c-8112-0290f8eda65f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Block Diagonalization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "109d2983-4b0d-59a7-b46d-9bf5c8b39a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372912} {:answer/id #uuid "eff4f0c3-5ff3-52e3-8235-1774ac92fc5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372913} {:answer/id #uuid "979669bf-4fd3-574f-a43a-f9099f9b478b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372914} {:answer/id #uuid "973f1f0d-c096-50e4-af48-53cd318a5a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372915} {:answer/id #uuid "b9fc3a76-1f34-5dc1-b068-48fe031dc91a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eff4f0c3-5ff3-52e3-8235-1774ac92fc5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372913} :answer-field/id #uuid "a603b3a9-798a-5e0d-98d9-1dd22f0ac7a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4156fed3-f50c-5889-96b0-00df60d067cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-135533" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a block diagonal matrix $B,$ where the $2\\times 2$ block represents a rotation-scaling matrix, such that $A=PB{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A$ is a real $3\\times 3$ matrix that has one real eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}$ with corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and two complex eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{3}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{3},$ then $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) \\\\ 0 & -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & \\text{Re}({v}_{2}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nTo compute the eigenvalues of $A,$ we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-3-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-2(-10)) & =0 \\\\ (-3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-12\\lambda +52) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the real eigenvalue is \n${\\lambda }_{1}=-3.$\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{2,3} & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{(-12)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{-64}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm 8\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =6\\pm 4\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the block diagonal matrix is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d4c1a7b-2341-5b8c-8112-0290f8eda65f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Block Diagonalization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c05fc026-0240-5afa-98f2-26fa1ce711d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372919} {:answer/id #uuid "e22b9609-b46e-555a-b8ad-a926c4790900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372920} {:answer/id #uuid "19291d1a-8143-5055-8ff9-8b78e36a5dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372921} {:answer/id #uuid "fbce385b-f908-599b-bfa0-8b4df8afdd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372922} {:answer/id #uuid "1adb60e1-af5b-5215-b2d9-2d373c3f0215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19291d1a-8143-5055-8ff9-8b78e36a5dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372921} :answer-field/id #uuid "506a5f31-6403-5b50-9e6a-d85a624536d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f033340-221b-5ef9-95cd-6f41dddc0d1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-135534" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a block diagonal matrix $B,$ where the $2\\times 2$ block represents a rotation-scaling matrix, such that $A=PB{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A$ is a real $3\\times 3$ matrix that has one real eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}$ with corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and two complex eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{3}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{3},$ then $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) \\\\ 0 & -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & \\text{Re}({v}_{2}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nTo compute the eigenvalues of $A,$ we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 4-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )((-2-\\lambda )^{2}-5(-5)) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +29) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the real eigenvalue is \n${\\lambda }_{1}=4.$\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{2,3} & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{(4)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 29}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{-100}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm 10\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =-2\\pm 5\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the block diagonal matrix is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5ccd12c-a814-5ebb-985c-eef8707001f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Invertible Matrix in Block Diagonal Form of an NxN Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76b2d52f-4f21-5fde-b896-a63aa98919a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372926} {:answer/id #uuid "93ac6601-29e2-5ff7-8fcf-7de279fe36fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -6 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372927} {:answer/id #uuid "82d9952e-ea5b-5f24-b313-e32cbbc80964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 4 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372928} {:answer/id #uuid "e7212309-724e-5e67-b0d0-be4e200acf60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372929} {:answer/id #uuid "0be8b3f1-3590-5937-879c-b1e8eab09766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & -2 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82d9952e-ea5b-5f24-b313-e32cbbc80964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 4 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372928} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bf7552c-32fc-545e-9e3e-1d3cb1fbf75b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bff3fdd4-73ae-5244-844a-4df0d111ce8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-135536" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ and the block diagonal matrix $B$ shown below, where both $2\\times 2$ blocks of $B$ represent rotation-scaling matrices:\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3+4\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\text{i} \\\\ -7+4\\text{i} \\\\ -6+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2-6\\text{i} \\\\ -3+2\\text{i} \\\\ -6+\\text{i} \\\\ -5-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are the eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3-7\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=2-4\\text{i},$ respectively. \nGiven that $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ which of the following could be the matrix $P?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ real matrix that has complex eigenvalues \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{4}$ \n\nwith corresponding eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{3}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{4},$ \n\nthen $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{1}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{1}) & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{1}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{1}) & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{3}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{3}) \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{3}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{3})\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ \\text{Re}({v}_{1}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{1}) & \\text{Re}({v}_{3}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nFrom our block diagonal matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe deduce that the first and second columns of $P$ correspond to the complex eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and the third and forth columns of $P$ correspond to the complex eigenvector ${v}_{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 4 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372931 :knowle